#doc (Manual) "Subrepresentation" =>
# Subrepresentation
%%%
tag := "Chapter2/Definition2.3.4"
number := false
%%%
*Definition 2.3.4.* A *subrepresentation* of a representation $`V` of an algebra $`A` is a subspace $`W \subset V` which is invariant under all the operators $`\rho(a) : V \to V`, $`a \in A`.

For instance, $`0` and $`V` are always subrepresentations.
